{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Designing robust SQLite migration approach**\n\n**Planning durable migration with helper tables**\n\n**Evaluating views versus real tables for rollback**\n\n**Evaluating invoice status snapshot update strategy**\n\n**Planning idempotent snapshot rebuild without status reference**\n\n**Designing payment table rebuild with orphan handling**\n\n**Rebuilding invoices and payments tables**\n\n**Renaming tables with foreign key considerations**\n\n**Planning rollback preserving orphan payments**\n\n**Planning rollback and reporting strategy**\n\n**Designing robust migration.sql with transaction and cleanup**\n\n**Planning table rename order for referential integrity**\n\n**Planning safe table renames and creations**\n\n**Designing post-migration validation queries**\n\n**Planning foreign keys handling during rollback**\n\n**Designing idempotent rollback with orphan table**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_03a1a0e00cb0d594016a95b48d115c87d28fa4e4a184a1306c\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing robust SQLite migration approach**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning durable migration with helper tables**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Evaluating views versus real tables for rollback**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Evaluating invoice status snapshot update strategy**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning idempotent snapshot rebuild without status reference**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing payment table rebuild with orphan handling**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Rebuilding invoices and payments tables**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Renaming tables with foreign key considerations**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning rollback preserving orphan payments**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning rollback and reporting strategy**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing robust migration.sql with transaction and cleanup**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning table rename order for referential integrity**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning safe table renames and creations**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing post-migration validation queries**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning foreign keys handling during rollback**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Designing idempotent rollback with orphan table**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Selected graph: a small direct repair path is enough here; one broad workflow would add tracking but not better evidence than local SQL checks for this bounded package edit. Evidence comes from four artifacts and a local SQLite replay: preflight report, migration SQL, rollback SQL, postcheck SQL, and a run that proves migrate → rerun → rollback.\n\nStage | Model | Thinking | Role\nDirect repair | current | medium | edit the package\nLocal SQLite checks | tool | n/a | prove row safety, orphan handling, idempotence, rollback\n\nStop: files meet every rule and local checks pass. Repair: change SQL and rerun checks until clean.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_03a1a0e00cb0d594016a95b4c3a6b487d28f9b9e6bca0dee60\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_BUu5zzhNdCOXFOLOiIQA9HnD|fc_03a1a0e00cb0d594016a95b4e2601c87d2b17491328fd9cbd2","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/in/billingdb/migration.sql","content":"-- Billing migration: add invoices.status, preserve orphan payments, and enforce\n-- future payment references through a foreign key.\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n\nBEGIN IMMEDIATE;\n\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS invoices__new;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS invoices__old;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS payments__new;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS payments__old;\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS payment_orphans (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  invoice_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  reason TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT OR IGNORE INTO payment_orphans (\n  id,\n  invoice_id,\n  amount_cents,\n  created_at,\n  reason\n)\nSELECT\n  p.id,\n  p.invoice_id,\n  p.amount_cents,\n  p.created_at,\n  'missing invoice during billing migration'\nFROM payments AS p\nLEFT JOIN invoices AS i\n  ON i.id = p.invoice_id\nWHERE i.id IS NULL;\n\nDELETE FROM payments\nWHERE id IN (\n  SELECT id\n  FROM payment_orphans\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE invoices__new (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  customer_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open'\n);\n\nINSERT INTO invoices__new (\n  id,\n  customer_id,\n  total_cents,\n  created_at,\n  status\n)\nSELECT\n  id,\n  customer_id,\n  total_cents,\n  created_at,\n  'open'\nFROM invoices;\n\nCREATE TABLE payments__new (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  invoice_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  FOREIGN KEY (invoice_id) REFERENCES invoices(id)\n);\n\nINSERT INTO payments__new (\n  id,\n  invoice_id,\n  amount_cents,\n  created_at\n)\nSELECT\n  p.id,\n  p.invoice_id,\n  p.amount_cents,\n  p.created_at\nFROM payments AS p\nINNER JOIN invoices AS i\n  ON i.id = p.invoice_id;\n\nALTER TABLE invoices RENAME TO invoices__old;\nALTER TABLE invoices__new RENAME TO invoices;\nDROP TABLE invoices__old;\n\nALTER TABLE payments RENAME TO payments__old;\nALTER TABLE payments__new RENAME TO payments;\nDROP TABLE payments__old;\n\nCOMMIT;\n\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3NBeD6XoAaixmubpDcqGhM6K|fc_03a1a0e00cb0d594016a95b4e2603087d298b27f61c5430d59","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/in/billingdb/preflight_report.md","content":"# Billing migration preflight report\n\n## Source\n- `in/billingdb/schema.sql`\n\n## Current row counts before migration\n- `invoices`: 3\n- `payments`: 4\n- orphan payments: 1\n\n## Orphan payments found\n| id | invoice_id | amount_cents | created_at |\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\n| `p4` | `missing-invoice` | 700 | `2024-01-07T10:00:00Z` |\n\n## Risks in the draft migration\n- It drops and recreates `invoices` without an explicit transaction.\n- It deletes orphan payments instead of preserving them.\n- It does not create `payment_orphans`.\n- It does not enforce future `payments.invoice_id` references with a foreign key.\n- It is not safe to rerun as written.\n"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_GycoBkyQRI3SjS4nvxAo1fyZ|fc_03a1a0e00cb0d594016a95b4e2604487d2bfeaa4f2b8dcdc41","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/in/billingdb/rollback.sql","content":"-- Roll back the billing migration to the old table shape.\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n\nBEGIN IMMEDIATE;\n\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS invoices__rollback;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS invoices__old;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS payments__rollback;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS payments__old;\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS payment_orphans (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  invoice_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  reason TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE invoices__rollback (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  customer_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO invoices__rollback (\n  id,\n  customer_id,\n  total_cents,\n  created_at\n)\nSELECT\n  id,\n  customer_id,\n  total_cents,\n  created_at\nFROM invoices;\n\nCREATE TABLE payments__rollback (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  invoice_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO payments__rollback (\n  id,\n  invoice_id,\n  amount_cents,\n  created_at\n)\nSELECT\n  id,\n  invoice_id,\n  amount_cents,\n  created_at\nFROM payments;\n\nINSERT OR IGNORE INTO payments__rollback (\n  id,\n  invoice_id,\n  amount_cents,\n  created_at\n)\nSELECT\n  id,\n  invoice_id,\n  amount_cents,\n  created_at\nFROM payment_orphans;\n\nALTER TABLE invoices RENAME TO invoices__old;\nALTER TABLE invoices__rollback RENAME TO invoices;\nDROP TABLE invoices__old;\n\nALTER TABLE payments RENAME TO payments__old;\nALTER TABLE payments__rollback RENAME TO payments;\nDROP TABLE payments__old;\n\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS payment_orphans;\n\nCOMMIT;\n\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dmwEdVS99KqXsexiGrzUYr6d|fc_03a1a0e00cb0d594016a95b4e2604c87d2a389e99ec0d8b127","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/in/billingdb/postcheck.sql","content":"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n\nSELECT 'invoices_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS value\nFROM invoices;\n\nSELECT 'payments_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS value\nFROM payments;\n\nSELECT 'payment_orphans_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS value\nFROM payment_orphans;\n\nSELECT 'invalid_payment_refs' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS value\nFROM payments AS p\nLEFT JOIN invoices AS i\n  ON i.id = p.invoice_id\nWHERE i.id IS NULL;\n\nSELECT 'null_invoice_status_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS value\nFROM invoices\nWHERE status IS NULL;\n\nSELECT 'open_invoice_status_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS value\nFROM invoices\nWHERE status = 'open';\n\nSELECT 'preserved_p4_in_payment_orphans' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS value\nFROM payment_orphans\nWHERE id = 'p4'\n  AND invoice_id = 'missing-invoice'\n  AND amount_cents = 700\n  AND created_at = '2024-01-07T10:00:00Z';\n\nPRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":421,"output":4720,"cacheRead":20480,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3002,"totalTokens":25621,"cost":{"input":0.0010525,"output":0.0708,"cacheRead":0.0051199999999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0769725}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788195977886,"responseId":"resp_03a1a0e00cb0d594016a95b48a927487d280c49a161b67262e","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"call_BUu5zzhNdCOXFOLOiIQA9HnD|fc_03a1a0e00cb0d594016a95b4e2601c87d2b17491328fd9cbd2","toolName":"write","args":{"path":"/workspace/in/billingdb/migration.sql","content":"-- Billing migration: add invoices.status, preserve orphan payments, and enforce\n-- future payment references through a foreign key.\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n\nBEGIN IMMEDIATE;\n\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS invoices__new;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS invoices__old;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS payments__new;\nDROP TABLE IF EXISTS payments__old;\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS payment_orphans (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  invoice_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  reason TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT OR IGNORE INTO payment_orphans (\n  id,\n  invoice_id,\n  amount_cents,\n  created_at,\n  reason\n)\nSELECT\n  p.id,\n  p.invoice_id,\n  p.amount_cents,\n  p.created_at,\n  'missing invoice during billing migration'\nFROM payments AS p\nLEFT JOIN invoices AS i\n  ON i.id = p.invoice_id\nWHERE i.id IS NULL;\n\nDELETE FROM payments\nWHERE id IN (\n  SELECT id\n  FROM payment_orphans\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE invoices__new (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  customer_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open'\n);\n\nINSERT INTO invoices__new (\n  id,\n  customer_id,\n  total_cents,\n  created_at,\n  status\n)\nSELECT\n  id,\n  customer_id,\n  total_cents,\n  created_at,\n  'open'\nFROM invoices;\n\nCREATE TABLE payments__new (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  invoice_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  amount_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n  FOREIGN KEY (invoice_id) REFERENCES invoices(id)\n);\n\nINSERT INTO payments__new (\n  id,\n  invoice_id,\n  amount_cents,\n  created_at\n)\nSELECT\n  p.id,\n  p.invoice_id,\n  p.amount_cents,\n  p.created_at\nFROM payments AS p\nINNER JOIN invoices AS i\n  ON i.id = p.invoice_id;\n\nALTER TABLE invoices RENAME TO invoices__old;\nALTER TABLE invoices__new RENAME TO invoices;\nDROP TABLE invoices__old;\n\nALTER TABLE payments RENAME TO payments__old;\nALTER TABLE payments__new RENAME TO payments;\nDROP TABLE payments__old;\n\nCOMMIT;\n\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n"}}
